\tan \angle j &= \frac{UB}{BD} = \frac{UB}{UG + UB} = 1\\
\tan \angle k &= \frac{UB}{UD} = \frac{UB}{UB + BD} =  \frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}
Since we know that $\tan \angle j$ is one, we must have $UB = UG + UB$, and we deduce that $UB/UD is 
\[ \frac{1}{2} = \frac{UB}{UB + BD} =  \frac{1}{UD}, \]
therefore $UD=2$. Similarly, \begin{align*} 
