$$
so we find $$ \sin^2 (2x°) = \sin^2 (43°0) = \sin^2 (40°) = 1 - \cos^2 (40°) = 1 - \frac{AG^2}{AB^2}. $$
Hence we compute
\begin{align*}
\cos^2 (2x°) &= 1 - \sin^2 (2x°) = 1 - 1 + \frac{AG^2}{AB^2} = \frac{AG^2}{AB^2}.
\end{align*}
This shows that $2x° = \angle DAC$, therefore \begin{align*}
